From 5a1be217df3d5155e3445a723349e80491e8465b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:40:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 39/43] pco: raise max_unroll_iterations further to 256 for
 loops longer than 64 iterations

c2bde57 raised the unroll threshold from 16 to 64 and removed the cliff at 16. A probe
with a 128-iteration loop shows the same cliff recurs above the new limit:

  cstpi128 (128 iterations), limit 64:   7.4 M inv/s
  cstpi    (32 iterations),  limit 64:  72.4 M inv/s

cstpi128 runs four times the iterations, so equal efficiency would be about 72.4/4 =
18.1 M inv/s. At 7.4 it was 2.4x less efficient per iteration - the loop was not fully
unrolled at 64.

At 256 the 128-iteration loop reaches 19.5 M inv/s (2.64x), which is the equal-
efficiency figure, so the cliff is gone. 32-iteration probes are unchanged, as they must
be since they were already fully unrolled.

  probe                 limit 64   limit 256   limit 1024
  cstpi128 (128 iters)  7.4        19.5        19.6
  cstpi    (32 iters)   72.4       72.0        70.3
  cstpf    (32 iters)   84.6       84.6        88.3
  vkheavy               255.8 ms   -           255.3 ms

1024 shows no gain over 256 for the measured case, so 256 is chosen: the smallest value
that removes the measured cliff. Larger values increase code size, which is the
trade-off, and that is why the limit is not raised arbitrarily high.

Correctness green: vkrender 512 and 2048, bda, vk13, pctest, vk16, and glmark2-es2
--validate 27 scenes.
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
index 8822523..4a345d1 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ static const nir_shader_compiler_options nir_options = {
 
    .lower_helper_invocation = true,
 
-   .max_unroll_iterations = 64,
+   .max_unroll_iterations = 256,
    .max_samples = 4,
 
    .io_options = nir_io_vectorizer_ignores_types,
